We have FB with inputs RequestBtn, ServiceReady, Busy, Cancel, outputs Pending, RequestLamp, Dispatched. Internal PrevCall? Requirement says "internal PrevCall are FALSE" likely previous button history variable named PrevCall. The LTL def uses pre.preButton. We can name internal PrevCall? Requirement 1: "Initially Pending, RequestLamp, Dispatched and internal PrevCall are FALSE. Update the previous RequestBtn value every scan, including cancellation scans." So use PrevCall as previous RequestBtn. Need preserve interface names exactly. Need implement.

Logic:
Every scan:
rise := RequestBtn AND NOT PrevCall;
request := Pending OR rise; (previous pending OR current button rise) But note Cancel priority: request maybe computed before cancellation, but dispatch/pending gated by !Cancel.
canServe := ServiceReady AND NOT Busy.
If Cancel TRUE:
 Pending := FALSE; Dispatched := FALSE; RequestLamp := FALSE? Requirement 2 clear Pending and Dispatched, still update button history. P03 RequestLamp always equals Pending. So RequestLamp := Pending (FALSE). 
Else:
 if request AND canServe: Dispatched := TRUE; Pending := FALSE.
 else: Dispatched := FALSE; Pending := request (preserve unconsumed). If request false then pending false. Requirement 3: "If Request AND ServiceReady AND NOT Busy, set Dispatched=TRUE and Pending=FALSE for this scan. Otherwise set Dispatched=FALSE and preserve an unconsumed request in Pending. Busy must not lose a request, even when ServiceReady=TRUE. RequestLamp always equals Pending."
Need set RequestLamp := Pending always after pending update.
PrevCall := RequestBtn at end (including cancel).
Need consider exact scan semantics: "Let Request=previous_Pending OR current_button_rise." previous_Pending means Pending at beginning of scan. So use old Pending variable before modification. In ST, output Pending retains previous value at entry. Need compute request before assigning Pending. In ST within FB, Pending is variable. We can do:
